r-spacing:1.5px\"><strong>&nbsp;AFTER&nbsp;</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4',serif;font-size:19px\"><strong>What the click trains, session after session</strong></span></p><p>✓ Holding lag through the bottom of the swing</p><p>✓ More compressed, consistent ball striking</p><p>✓ Straighter flight, tighter dispersion</p><p>✓ More solid strikes with the same effort</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggA6TxB0001_text","label":"ggA6TxB0001_text","default":"<p>It’s worth saying the quiet part out loud: this isn’t new physics. Coaches have taught lag and release timing for a hundred years. What’s new is feeling it happen in your own hands without paying for a studio session.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggA6OffT001_text","label":"ggA6OffT001_text","default":"<p><span style=\"color:#B5813A\"><strong>30% off</strong></span> plus free shipping on $50+ orders.</p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggA6OffB001_label","label":"ggA6OffB001_label","default":"<p>SEE TODAY’S OFFER →</p>"}],
